/* Authored mascot frames: the DANCE loop (after the glowing flower). A lopsided jelly bounce-and-sway on the ground: plant, crouch right, hop up leaning right,
   land squashed leaning left, hop up leaning left, settle. Hand-finished whole-pixel frames, NOT the CSS rotate: the lower body bends under a head that rides
   with the face, and the lumps follow through a beat late (the left nub and the belly roll keep swinging the old way for one frame: f0 nub out left after the
   left hop, f4/f5 nub tucked and roll out right after the right hop). The left half of the loop (4-7) is its own frame set, not a flip of 1-3: the body keeps
   its heavy left sag and left nub whichever way it leans. Format: lintPoseFrames in tools/lint_mascot_body.mjs; checked by tools/lint_anim_dance.mjs.
   NON-baked: compose() draws the usual upright face at fcx,cy (pass happy:1 for the smile), the sprout and hats; feet are per frame.

   WIRING NOTE (os.js dance(), started from eatGlow() about two seconds after the awe line):
   - Beat table, one loop = 1080 ms, play it 5 times (5400 ms, the old call asks for 5200) (no flip; flip:1 on every beat mirrors the whole dance, which also lints green):
       frame  hold   flip  what                                           body / feet
       0      150    0     plant, rest-ish (breath body)                  planted, body ends row 41, feet on 42-43
       1      120    0     crouch: squash S1, lean right                  planted, weight on the right foot
       2      120    0     take-off: stretch T2, lean right               2 px up (body ends row 39), feet tucked, 2 px off the ground
       3      150    0     peak, tilted further right                     2 px up, feet dangle (left 2 px, right 1 px off the ground)
       4      130    0     land: squash S2, lean left, lumps still right  planted, wide feet
       5      120    0     take-off: stretch T2, lean left                2 px up, feet tucked
       6      150    0     peak, tilted further left                      2 px up, left foot dangles lower
       7      140    0     settle: squash S1, lean left                   planted (loops back to 0)
     e.g. const D=[150,120,120,150,130,120,150,140],frames=[];for(let t=0;t<ms;t+=1080)D.forEach((h,i)=>frames.push([{pose:'dance:'+i,flip:0,happy:1,
       face:0,mouth:0,hop:0,dx:0,heart:i===3||i===6?1:0},h]));frames.push([RESET,0]);play(frames);
   - It replaces the rAF loop that set bcv.style.transform='translateX(..) rotate(..)': delete that loop (a CSS rotate of a 2-3x canvas breaks the pixel grid and
     the sway is now drawn). stopDance() can stay as is (it cancels nothing harmful and clears the transform). If you want him to travel, use dx (whole canvas px,
     at most +-1: the lint checks the frames fit the canvas with dx -1..1), not translateX. Keep air:0 on every beat (the ground shadow stays put while he hops).
   - RESET must clear pose and flip (pose:null,flip:0); stage and hat from BS pass through (sprout stage 4 and both hats fit on every frame).
   - Reduced motion: no loop. Show frame 0 with happy:1, heart:1 ({pose:'dance:0',happy:1,heart:1}) for the whole ms, then RESET. Today play() runs before the
     reduce check, so move the check above it. */
