/* Authored frames: the dead old Mac (the little red computer with the crossed-out face that look.mac=1 draws in composeMac) falling over, cracking and smoking,
   drawn at every angle so the OS no longer rotates the canvas with CSS. Method: the tilted casings were drafted at exact pixel slopes (so every straight edge is
   one run length: 3 px on 1 and 3, 1 px on 2), every edge run was audited, the square corners were trimmed by hand and each casing is point-symmetric about its
   centre; frame 1's screen outline is listed edge by edge, frame 3's screen, face and slot are frame 1's mirrored and given an exact quarter turn, and the faces,
   slots, vents, cracks, smoke and shadows are placed pixel by pixel. Lint: tools/lint_anim_mac.mjs (lintPoseFrames rules plus the checks in its header).
   Every frame is baked:true with feet:[] (compose() iterates feet). The body rows v are the casing only (closed 1 px ink outline, p on the edges that face up or
   left, R on the edges that face down or right: the light stays at the top left while the Mac turns); everything else is the over layer: the screen, the face,
   the floppy slot and vent, the cracks, the smoke, the spark and the ground shadow.
   The tilts use exact pixel slopes, not the nominal angles: 1 is 18.4 deg (3:1 steps), 2 is 45 deg (1:1), 3 is 71.6 deg (1:3), 4 is 90 deg (an exact quarter turn).
   All frames turn clockwise (falling to the right) about the Mac's centre, the canvas point (16,29) (the pixel corner between columns 15/16 and rows 28/29), so the
   caller keeps one anchor. flip:1 mirrors a frame for a fall to the left.

   WIRING NOTE (os.js unrTryAgain, the crash sequence after "Try again"; today it draws look.mac=1 and turns the canvas with style.transform rotate()):
   - flip:0 for the fall as it is today (clockwise, to the right). flip:1 is a different icon (the vent swaps sides), so never flip frame 0 against look.mac.
   - os.js has one Mac use (unrTryAgain, around line 1941) and no intro path; its land formula assumes the CSS-rotated canvas, which the row numbers below replace.
   - Draw with compose({pose:'mac:'+i, flip, dir:[0,0], stage:0, air:1}). Always air:1: frames 0 and 4 to 8 carry their own ground shadow, 1 to 3 are in the air.
     Frame 0 is pixel-identical to composeMac, so BS.mac=1 can become pose 'mac:0' with no visible jump. Drop the CSS rotate(); keep only translate for the fall.
   - The lowest Mac pixel: row 41 on frames 0 and 8 (as today), row 43 on 1 and 2, row 41 on 3, row 38 on 4 to 7 (lying, the Mac is 20 px tall about the same centre).
     So the landed Mac (4 to 7) sits 3 canvas px higher in its cell than the upright one: land the element 3 px x scale lower than an upright Mac on the same floor.
   - Pop in: frame 0, held through the existing 1000 ms wait.
   - Fall (about 400 ms, frames 0,1,2,3,4): pick the frame from the existing rot (0..90 deg) instead of rotating: rot<9 -> 0, <32 -> 1, <58 -> 2, <81 -> 3, else 4.
     Timed instead: 0 80 ms, 1 100 ms, 2 100 ms, 3 100 ms, then 4 on landing.
   - Thud: hold 4 through the bounce and about 200 ms after.
   - Crack and smoke (about 600 ms): 5 (first crack, 150 ms), 6 (crack across the screen, a crack in the casing, a puff, 200 ms), 7 (bigger puff risen, new puff,
     a yellow spark at the crack, 250 ms). The vortex can carry frame 7 (or 6) with its own spin transform as today.
   - Back to the mascot (the intro, or a crash without the vortex): 8 = the Mac back upright, cracked and smoking (one 160 ms pop from 7, no in-between needed);
     then the flicker: swap 8 and the mascot's rest pose every 60 to 90 ms, 3 to 4 times, ending on the mascot.
   - Reduced motion: frame 0 only (static, as today: the reduce path skips the fall). */
