/* Authored mascot frames: ROOT, the root launch, the root double jump, the airborne roots and the landing, drawn to the art director's
   concept sheet (ROOT LAUNCH, ROOT AIRBORNE, DOUBLE JUMP, LAND, FX/DETAILS rows). He keeps his own lumpy body (approved levels from mascot/body.js,
   unchanged, placed at the top of a TALL cell) and compose() still draws his face, cheeks, sprout and hat. The over layer carries what is new:
   chunky round boots (10x7: ink k, body U, light u on the heel and the toe cap, shade v, sole V; toe forward) and tan roots (3 to 4 px at the
   sole stepping down to 1 px; light u on the upper left, mid A, shade a, dark outline e; olive g then fresh green G at the curled tips),
   leaves, dirt clods (u A a in an e outline), root bits, lone specks (v, b) and brown dust (A u b). Authored FACING RIGHT; facing left =
   the same frame with flip:1.
   Format: lintPoseFrames in tools/lint_mascot_body.mjs; rules: tools/lint_anim_root.mjs. Extra frame fields: cellH (72, read by compose and
   the lint), name; sole = the frame's lowest sole (V) row; ground = 36 on the four ground frames, else null; shoes = the two boot boxes
   [x,y,w,h] (left boot first, cell coords, facing right).

   WIRING NOTE (the Wake Up game; os.js has no root jump, nothing there changes)
   THE CELL IS 32x72 (every frame sets cellH:72, compose returns 72 rows; paint() must draw all of them, not a fixed 48).
   Today render.js draws the plain 32x48 sprite at (p.x-7, p.y-20), the 8x5 SHOE at rows 39..43 of that cell (its sole on the box's last
   row p.y+PH-1) and strands() for the roots. While a root frame shows, draw it INSTEAD of shoes() and of strands()' loose strands:
   - cell: drawX = Math.round(p.x) - 7 - ox (unchanged), drawY = Math.round(p.y) + PH - 1 - ANIM_ROOT.soleRow - oy = Math.round(p.y) - 12 - oy.
     ANIM_ROOT.soleRow = 35: every frame's soles are on cell row 35, which lands on p.y+PH-1, exactly where today's SHOE sole is.
     ANIM_ROOT.groundRow = 36 (= p.y+PH) is the first row of ground: on the ground frames everything from row 36 down is IN the ground.
     Exceptions: dig sinks its soles 1 px into the ground (sole 36), hang dangles the back boot 1 px (36). The cell reaches 36 rows below
     the feet (rows 36..71) for the hanging roots; nothing is above row 0.
   - The boots sit at cell columns 6..15 and 17..26, rows 29..35 (today's shoes 8..15 and 18..25), so they stay over his feet. Each boot's top
     row lies on the body's second-last row. The body's last row is row 30 (dig 31), i.e. p.y+18; the plain sprite's is p.y+21, so switching to
     a root frame lifts the body 3 px (the boots are taller than today's).
   - look: compose({pose:'root:'+i, flip:p.face<0?1:0, dir:[p.face,vy<-1?-1:vy>2?1:0], air:1, stage, hat, face ...}). air:1 always, or
     compose draws the ground shadow through the roots. Faces, hats, sprout stages 0..4 and the mask work as on any pose frame.
   Frames (index name: game moment, hold in 60 Hz steps):
     0 crouch      ready: S1 squash, boots planted, root tips into the ground, two dirt mounds.   4 steps
     1 dig         deepest squash (S3), boots dug in 1 px, roots spread 20 rows into the ground,
                   clods flying up past his sides and over his head.                              4 steps
     2 push        T1 stretch leaving the ground, roots flung out sideways and down, specks.      3 steps, then rise1/rise2
     3 rise1       T1, two long root bundles trailing about a body height, forked, 3 leaves.    5 steps, alternate with 4 while rising
     4 rise2       T1 (other boil), shorter bundles swaying the other way, 2 leaves.            5 steps
     5 burst       THE DOUBLE JUMP: rest body; the boot roots join in a Y into one thick taproot that
                   forks wide below him (curled branches both sides), side shoots, 4 leaves, dirt ring.  b.t 0..3
     6 burst2      T1 stretched up: longer taproot, branches fully spread and spiralling, 4 leaves.     b.t 4..9
     7 hang        apex: rest body, two bundles swaying gently, back boot 1 px lower, 2 leaves.  while |vy| <= 1
     8 fall        falling: roots stream up past his sides to his head and curl out, leaves,
                   fall lines (b) above and below.                                               while vy > 1
     9 retract     boots toes-down, roots curl back up in hooks under the boots.                see below
    10 landBurst   impact: S2 squash, roots slam and splay into the ground, a big crown of clods
                   and root bits spraying up both sides and over his head.                       3 steps
    11 landSettle  S1, root stubs sinking into the ground, two brown dust puffs.               5 steps, then the plain sprite
   Picking them (engine facts: player.js fires the root jump only in the air, `jump(p,RJV,ev,'root')`, and pushes
   S.roots {x:p.x+PW/2, y:p.y+PH, t, g, hit}; burst() counts b.t per step, its hit box grows until t 10, render.js back() draws the
   strands in from t 18 over 10 steps or 5 steps after landing (b.g), and the burst is dropped at t 30):
     with a live burst b and !p.ground:  b.t < 4 -> 5;  b.t < 10 -> 6;  b.t >= 18, or about to land -> 9; else by vy: vy < -1 -> 3/4
       alternating every 5 steps; vy > 1 -> 8; else 7. ("about to land": player.js landing() is not exported; export it, or test in render
       that vy > 0 and solid ground is within about 8 px under the box.)
     on the 'land' event within 20 steps of a root jump (or while b.g < 5): p.land (set to 8, counts down 1 per step) 8..6 -> 10, 5..1 -> 11.
     the ROOT LAUNCH (0, 1, 2) has no trigger today: there is no grounded root jump. Use it for the seed pickup demo (demo() jumps at k 24),
       a future charged root launch (0 for 4 steps, 1 for 4, the jump on 2, then 3/4), or play 2 alone for 3 steps on an ordinary jump
       while S.items.root.
   Mismatch to know about: the burst's hit box (8+t*.9 each side, 6+t*3 deep: about 17 px each side and 36 px down at t 10) now matches the
   drawn burst roots well (16 px each side, 34 rows down), but strands() bends a strand onto a gripped enemy and baked frames cannot: keep
   strands() for the gripping strands only (hold != null), drawn behind the frame.
   ROOT_FX particles (stamp rows at a world point; '.' clear; anchor = the sprite's bottom-centre unless noted; cell anchors are facing
   right, mirror them as 31-x when flipped, then world = (drawX + x, drawY + y)):
     piece  (12x10 curvy forked twig, 2 frames, swap every 4 steps): 2 at burst (5) from the soles (11,36) and (22,36), vx +-0.8, vy -1.5,
            gravity .15; 2 more at landBurst (10) from (4,36) and (27,36).
     leaf   (7x5, 3 frames, every 6 steps, a twirl): at burst2 (6) from the curled outer tips (4,63) and (27,63); drift vy +.3, vx sin wobble.
     crumbs (8x6, 3 frames, every 3 steps; isolated specks intended): at dig (1) and landBurst (10) beside the boots (3,35) and (28,35);
            1 under the fan at burst (5) at (16,70).
     dust   (10x8, 4 frames, 4 steps each, grows then dithers away): at landSettle (11) on the ground at (3,36) and (28,36).
     lines  (6x10, 3 frames, 3 steps each; top-left anchor): during a long fall (8), beside the head at (0,0) and (26,0).
   Timer playback (a cutscene or the OS, setTimeout per pose): crouch 70 ms, dig 70, push 50, rise1/rise2 90 each, burst 70, burst2 100,
   hang 140, fall 120, retract 80, landBurst 60, landSettle 110. Reduced motion: show 7 hang (one static pose, no FX).
   Every frame has roots with fresh green tips (crouch and landSettle only stubs); roots hang 22..36 rows below the soles on 3, 5, 6, 7. */
