/* Authored mascot frames: trash, the head-first dive into the Trash can, hand-drawn so the OS no longer rotates the canvas with CSS (rotate() tears the pixels).
   Format: lintPoseFrames in tools/lint_mascot_body.mjs; tools/lint_anim_trash.mjs has the extra rules. Drawn with compose({pose:'trash:<i>',flip,dir:[0,0],stage:0,air:1}).

   HOW THEY ARE DRAWN. Every frame is T2 (the 'stretch' body) turned CLOCKWISE about the body centre (15.5, 29.5), so the sprite turns in place and frame 0 sits
   pixel for pixel where the T2 stretch pose sits. Then redrawn by hand: the lumps ride round with the turn (two-bump head with its dip, the left nub, the belly roll, the
   droop), and the light stays in the world (highlight upper left, shade lower right), as in mascot/lean.js. He is WORRIED, never angry (he is being thrown away): wide open 6x7
   eyes with the pupils down, 3 px brows slanting up toward the middle (inner ends higher), the wobbly FACES.worry mouth and, in frames 0..3, a sweat bead 'T'
   flying off beside the head (world-upright, it is a drop). The face turns rigidly with the body (45 and 135 degrees: eye boxes kept upright, pupils, brows
   and mouth turned), so upside down the brows are under the eyes, the pupils at the top and the mouth above. A 2 px stem 'n' grows from the head top. All frames are baked:true: compose draws no face, sprout, hat or cheeks on top (see LIMITS).
   flip:1 mirrors a frame: the same pose turned ANTI-clockwise, with the lumps and highlight mirrored, exactly as the approved lean -1..-3 frames are.

   FRAMES (index: pose; canvas rows of body / feet / eye whites / stem):
     0  ready to dive: upright T2, worried face looking down, sweat bead, feet together under the belly.         body 18..41, feet 42..44, eyes 25..29, stem 16..17
     1  turning about 45 degrees: head up and to the right, feet trailing down-left.                            body 18..41, feet 34..41 (cols 0..9)
     2  about 90 degrees: on his side, head to the right, feet tucked in at his left side.                      body 19..40, feet cols 2..3
     3  about 135 degrees: head down and to the right, feet up and to the left.                                 body 17..40, feet 15..23
     4  180 degrees, upside down, diving: KICK A (his world-left foot kicked high, the right one tucked).       body 18..41, feet 15..17, eyes 30..34, stem 42..43
     5  180 degrees, KICK B (the other way round).                                                              body 18..41, feet 14..17, eyes 30..34, stem 42..43
     6  rummage tilt, about 170 degrees (10 degrees short of upside down), own feet.                            body 18..42, feet 14..16, eyes 29..35, stem 42..43
     7  rummage tilt, about 190 degrees (10 past; lopsided, not a mirror of 6).                                 body 18..41, feet 15..18, eyes 29..35, stem 41..42
   Upside down (4..7) the HEAD is at the BOTTOM of the canvas: feet at rows 14..18, the belly and droop at rows 18..~27, the eyes from row 29, the head bumps at 39..42.

   WIRING NOTE (os.js; the OS plays poses with setTimeout). Pose looks: {pose:'trash:<i>', flip:<0|1>, air:1}. Travelling right use flip:0, travelling left flip:1.
   binShow (an icon dragged into the Trash):
     - the three hops over: unchanged.
     - the flip, today `anim(220, rot(180*k))`: play 0 (90 ms, the wind-up at the top of the last hop), then 1, 2, 3, 4 at 55 ms each (220 ms). Drop the CSS rotate and
       transformOrigin. The drawn frames turn about the body centre (row 29.5), CSS turned about the canvas centre (row 24): upside down, the drawn body sits 12 canvas
       rows LOWER than the rotated canvas did (rows 18..41, not 6..29). So subtract 12*s px from top, s = bh/48, ramping in over the flip (top - 12*s*k).
     - going in and the rummage: the head is now at the bottom of the canvas, so the clip moves from the top edge to the BOTTOM edge. Exactly equivalent to today:
         top = topIn + d - 12*s;   clipPath = 'inset(0 0 ' + max(0, round(d - 12*s)) + 'px 0)'   (the rim stays at topIn + bh, as now)
       with today's d (fo*.55*k*k going in; fo*(.58+.2*sin) rummaging; fo*.78*(1-k) climbing out). Keep the 4 px left-right wobble; replace rot(180+11*sin) with frames:
       cycle 4, 6, 5, 7 (kick A, tilt, kick B, tilt) at 110 ms each for as long as the rummage lasts.
     - climbing out (today rot(180) then rot(180+180*k) while hopping left): hold 4/5 alternating at 110 ms while d runs down, then for the 380 ms hop play
       flip:1 frames 3, 2, 1 (the turn carries on clockwise past 180: 225, 270, 315 degrees, head leading to the left) at 70 ms each, then the existing
       stretch/idle play(). Top during the hop: today's arc minus 12*s*(1-k). (Or, simpler, unflipped 3, 2, 1, 0: he turns back the way he came.)
       Going from flip:0 rummage frames to flip:1 3, 2, 1 swaps the lumps for one frame; play the rummage and the climb-out at flip:1 when the exit goes left.
   trashDive (the mascot himself dropped on the Trash): today stretch pose, slide over (150 ms), drop in feet first (280 ms, bottom clip).
     - the slide: frame 0 (instead of the stretch look), with hoverY raised to at most rimY - bh*45/48 so nothing (feet end at row 44) is below the rim yet.
     - the flip, UNCLIPPED and above the rim: 1, 2, 3, 4 at 55 ms (a short hop; the frames turn in place, so here no 12*s shift is needed). Do not flip during
       the clipped drop: today's hoverY puts the rim at canvas row ~38, so clip(t) would slice frames 1..3 (feet, lower eye, then most of the face).
     - the drop (280 ms): 4 and 5 alternating at 110 ms, with today's bottom clip(t) unchanged. The clip is only right once he is upside down (the head, at the
       canvas bottom, goes in first). The pop out of the can afterwards stays upright, as now.
   Reduced motion: neither sequence runs (trashDive drops him, binShow only waits). If one static pose is wanted, use frame 0.

   LIMITS. Baked frames carry no hat (a hat vanishes for the dive and comes back after) and no sprout stage: the 2 px stem shows at every stage, also stage 0,
   where the normal poses draw no sprout. compose() needs no change. */
