/* Authored mascot frames: walk. The locomotion set for the Wake Up player (provisional until the player-feel pass reports; the game adopts it later, nothing uses it yet).
   Format: see lintPoseFrames in tools/lint_mascot_body.mjs; rules: tools/lint_anim_walk.mjs. NON-baked frames: body rows only, last body row on row 41, feet on rows 42..43
   (a lifted foot is a 1-row foot on row 42 or 41, lifted 1 or 2 px), and compose() draws the face at fcx,cy, so the caller still adds dir, face ('scared' ...), hat and sprout stage.
   Authored FACING RIGHT; facing left = the same frame with flip:1. Every frame is an approved body level redrawn, so the lumps travel with the pose:
   the rows from the head down through the right bulge (both bumps, the nub, the shoulder step) are shifted 1 px into travel (the lean), the roll grows 1 px forward and
   the droop stays behind, so the frames are 23 px wide; the bob is the level (contact = rest, down = breath, pass = T1).

   WIRING NOTE (game, not the OS: os.js has no walk and nothing there changes)
   - Cycle, frames 0..5, driven by distance, never by time:  frame = floor(d / WALK_STRIDE_PX) mod 6,  d = grounded distance travelled in ART pixels (the 32x48 sprite's
     pixels at the drawn scale; abs value, so it counts up walking either way). The planted foot moves back exactly WALK_STRIDE_PX (6) per frame, so at ANY speed there is
     no foot slide. Loops 5 -> 0. Reset d to 0 when a run starts from a standstill.
       0 contactA   rest body, front foot A out (heel strike), back foot B trailing (toe-off)
       1 downA      1 px lower (breath body), weight over foot A under the body, B lifted 2 px, peeling off behind
       2 passA      1 px higher (T1 body), A planted behind centre, B passes under the body, lifted
       3 contactB   as 0 with the feet swapped; its own drawing (the slosh boil variant, droop swung 1 px forward), not a mirror
       4 downB      as 1, feet swapped
       5 passB      as 2, feet swapped
     feet[0] is foot A and feet[1] foot B in every cycle frame. Planted feet (box x): A 23,17,11,5 in frames 0..3; B the same in frames 3,4,5,0.
   - 6 startLean: held for the first ~4 game steps of a run from a standstill while d keeps counting; after that, the cycle frame floor(d/6) mod 6, wherever that
     lands (the push-off frame hides the jump). Head leans ~6 degrees into travel (2 px at the top), back foot pushing off.
   - 7 stopSettle: the 1 px squash (S1 body, both feet planted, head still 1 px forward) for ~4 steps (about 70-100 ms) after the player stops, then the idle rest body.
   - 8 turn1, 9 turn2: the 3 steps before the facing flips on a reverse: turn1 for 1 step, turn2 for 2 steps, then flip and go on (skid frames, if any, come first).
     The body is 21 px wide (rest 22, the leaning walk frames 23) and the face anchor is 1 then 2 px toward the NEW facing (left, for these right-facing frames; with flip:1 they turn to the right).
     Pass dir:[-1,0] (unflipped) so the eyes lead the turn. hideCheek:-1 = the cheek on the authored left (the one at fcx-9..fcx-8; with flip:1 the mirrored one) should be
     hidden in the 3/4 view: compose() does not read this field yet, it still draws both cheeks (atlas.js would need to skip that cheek pair when the frame says so).
   - Hold times if ever played on a timer (OS or a cutscene): 90 ms per cycle frame (= 67 art px/s at 6 px per frame), startLean 120 ms, stopSettle 100 ms, turn 70 ms each.
   - Eyes: dir:[1,0] (unflipped) / [-1,0] (flipped) looks where he goes; 'scared' and both hats fit every frame, flipped or not (the lint checks it).
   - Reduced motion: the one static pose is walk:0 (contactA) while moving, the idle rest body when stopped. */
